Package: deecure
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: deep insight into every layer of a Linux computer, with safe fixes
 DeeCure reads every layer of your computer and explains it in plain
 English: sensors and their limits, PCIe links, firmware, the kernel,
 battery, memory, disks, services, network, and security. It warns about
 harm (heat, stalls, errors, wear), judged against each part's own
 limits, and never about normal use.
 .
 A small background agent collects data every minute, keeps a history,
 and runs rules that turn the data into findings such as "Main disk is
 low on space". A small root helper, started only when needed, makes
 admin changes after polkit asks for your password. The deecure command
 shows the findings in the terminal, and as JSON for scripts.
 .
 Everything stays on this computer. Nothing is sent anywhere.

Package: deecure-desktop
Architecture: any
Depends: deecure (= ${binary:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: libayatana-appindicator3-1
Description: desktop app for DeeCure
 The DeeCure window: a health score, problems explained in plain English,
 deep hardware details, live performance, battery and power controls,
 storage, services, logs, networks, security, privacy, an Optimize page,
 and safe fixes with undo, in Beginner, Advanced, and Expert views.
 .
 It shows what the deecure background agent collects. Everything stays
 on this computer. Nothing is sent anywhere.

